# antseal wire-registry freeze manifest — format version v1  (task Q50)
#
# `docs/format/registry-v1.md` IS format v1: it is the normative text a
# third-party verifier implements from, and `registry-v1.json` is its
# machine mirror. Everything else in the project that freezes — golden
# vectors, error codes, report bytes — freezes *relative to it*.
#
# Until this file existed, both were outside every freeze mechanism in the
# project. `scripts/vector-freeze.sh` covers `testdata/vectors/v<n>/*.json`
# only, and nothing pinned a byte of the registry.
#
# The consequence was sharpest for the 19 D10 parser caps. They are pinned
# by `format_registry_freeze::code_caps_match_the_registry`, which asserts
# in both directions that `codec::caps`'s constants equal the mirror's
# `caps.entries[].value`. That is a CONSISTENCY check, not a PIN: a
# coordinated edit of both files in one commit passes the entire suite,
# forever. Post-freeze that is a silent format change — and the caps decide
# whether a given `.sealproof` is a valid v1 bundle, which D84 §7 puts
# explicitly inside the freeze. The same shape covered every other registry
# fact: map keys, field names, reserved bands, scalar lengths, tuple
# arities, enum values, version dispatch. All were "code and JSON must
# agree"; none was "this value is X".
#
# This file is what makes a post-freeze change to either document a
# deliberate, reviewable act rather than an invisible one.
#
# This file is `sha256sum -c` compatible (lines starting with `#` are
# comments to GNU coreutils), so the digests can be checked with a tool
# that shares no code with antseal:
#
#     cd docs/format && grep -v '^#' FROZEN.sha256 | sha256sum -c -
#
# The authoritative checker is `crates/antseal-core/tests/format_freeze.rs`,
# driven by `scripts/format-freeze.sh`. Both reuse the directive parser and
# the manifest model of the Q6 vector freeze
# (`crates/antseal-core/tests/freeze_manifest/mod.rs`), so `#! status
# frozen` has exactly one meaning in this repo.
#
# ── directives (`#!`), parsed by the checker ────────────────────────────
#
#   manifest-version  this file's own schema version
#   format-version    the wire format version these documents define
#   status            pre-freeze | frozen
#   freeze-gate       the task that flips `status` to `frozen`
#
# `status frozen` (set at Q14): digests are permanent,
# `scripts/format-freeze.sh --update` refuses to modify or drop an entry,
# and an addition — a `registry-v2.*` pair — is the only legal change. A
# byte change to a frozen entry is a format-version event, never an edit
# (procedure Q27).
#
# The authority for that is Q14's own freeze act, NOT MVP-SPEC.md line 123
# (Q132). Line 123 is the *compatibility* rule — "every RELEASED
# manifest/bundle format version remains verifiable by all future CLI and
# page releases" — and D104 §1.5 measures with three independent
# confirmations that nothing has been released. Cited as the source of
# byte-immutability it is a conditional whose condition is false today, so a
# reader who checks it may conclude the freeze is soft: the inference D108 §3
# spends a section refusing. Q14 is deliberately STRONGER than line 123
# requires, and line 123 is what the freeze protects once a version ships.
#
#! manifest-version 1
#! format-version v1
#! status frozen
#! freeze-gate Q14
#
# ── frozen digests ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
2f576892e596715271bff96a194495f1579740ccd2d4ef61758ab3086c2da97d  registry-v1.json
